# generated by xcodegen — never commit (regenerated by build.sh)
*.xcodeproj/
# xcodebuild derivedData / output
build/
# staged cart sources (cart.c + data headers) + the staged AppIcon catalog, generated per
# target by build.sh / device.sh / build-app.js --ios. ALL of gen/ is build output.
# ⚠ gen/Assets.xcassets USED TO BE COMMITTED (the exception was "so a manual Xcode build, which
# runs no staging script, still gets an app icon"). That backfired: the catalog is REWRITTEN by
# every app build, so the committed copy was simply whoever staged last — it held pedalboard's
# icon — and it churned in `git status` forever. Worse, its mere existence disabled the
# reset-to-placeholder branch in both scripts (they tested for the file, not for a missing APP),
# so a single-cart build silently wore the previous app's icon. Untracked 2026-08-16.
# The placeholder still ships, as ios/default-icon.png; every scripted path stages the catalog
# from it (no APP) or from the manifest (APP=). The one case that loses out is a bare manual
# `xcodegen && xcodebuild` in a FRESH clone, which gets an actool warning about a missing AppIcon
# until you run any of the scripts once. That is the trade, and it is the right way round.
gen/*
# generated by xcodegen from project.yml (entitlements block / extension info plist)
*.entitlements
AU/Info.plist
# spike screenshots
snap*.png
# derived store spec (testflight.sh output)
project-store.yml
# xcodebuild output for the Mac Catalyst variant (ios/mac.sh)
build-mac/
AU/Info-mac.plist
Mac.entitlements
MacAU.entitlements
au-transport-check
rate-convert-check
build-test/
project-dev.yml
# derived Mac Catalyst spec (ios/mac.sh output — project-mac.yml + the app's AU identity)
project-mac-dev.yml
